-- title:
--   Lemma 3.17 (for $s+1$ polynomials) — the annihilator ideal is principal and generated by an irreducible
-- statement:
--   Let $s\in\mathbb N$ and $f_1,\dots,f_{s+1}\in\mathbb F[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ with $\operatorname{tr-deg}_{\mathbb F}(f)=s$. Then the ideal of annihilators
--   $$
--   \operatorname{Ann} f=\{A\in\mathbb F[y_1,\dots,y_{s+1}] : A(f_1,\dots,f_{s+1})=0\}
--   $$
--   is principal, generated by an irreducible polynomial.
--
--   The paper states it for $s=n$; the proof of Proposition 4.7 (p.27) applies it to $s+1$ polynomials in $n$ variables with transcendence degree $s$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: f₁, …, f_{n+1} ∈ F[x₁, …, x_n] with tr-deg(f) = n → f₁, …, f_{s+1} ∈ F[x₁, …, x_n] with tr-deg(f) = s, for every s; reason: s = n is the printed lemma; the general case is the form the proof of Proposition 4.7 uses, and it holds since Ann f is a height-one prime of the UFD F[y]
-- source:
--   Forbes and Staicu, Approximating Transcendence Degree in Medium Characteristic, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 3ab72a42…), Lemma 3.17, p.15 (as applied in the proof of Proposition 4.7, p.27)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TrDegJac_trDeg

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace TrDegJac

/-- **Lemma 3.17, for `s + 1` polynomials** — Forbes and Staicu, *Approximating Transcendence Degree in Medium Characteristic*, STOC 2027
submission (manuscript sha256 3ab72a42…), p.15:
"Let f₁, …, f_n, f_{n+1} ∈ F[x₁, …, x_n], with tr-deg(f) = n. Then the ideal of annihilators of f
is principal, and generated by an irreducible polynomial."

Stated for `s + 1` polynomials in `n` variables with `tr-deg(f) = s`, which is how the proof of
Proposition 4.7 (p.27) applies it; `s = n` is the printed lemma.

**Formalization Note.** The ideal of annihilators `Ann f` (p.7: "Ann f = ker φ(f)") is the kernel of
`MvPolynomial.aeval f : F[y₁, …, y_{s+1}] → F[x]`. -/
theorem lemma_3_17 {F : Type*} [Field F] {n s : ℕ} (f : Fin (s + 1) → MvPolynomial (Fin n) F)
    (hf : trDeg f = s) :
    ∃ A : MvPolynomial (Fin (s + 1)) F,
      Irreducible A ∧ RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.aeval f) = Ideal.span {A} := by sorry

end TrDegJac
